# NO END-OF-LINE CONVERSION, ANYWHERE. This is not a style preference.
#
# build_manifest.json records an md5 for every shipped file, and SETUP.cmd
# verifies the game files by md5 before it will replace anything. Git's default
# behaviour on Windows rewrites line endings on checkout, which would change the
# bytes of every .py, .ps1, .cmd and .txt in a clone - so `build_dist.py --check`
# would fail on all of them, and cdb would be handed a patch script that is not
# the one that was tested.
#
# A distribution whose whole contract is "these exact bytes" cannot let git
# normalise anything.
* -text
